# .mailmap - Normalizes author names in git log/blame/shortlog
#
# This file maps all variations of author names to a canonical form.
# Format: Canonical Name <canonical@email> Commit Name <commit@email>
#
# All commits will display as "nockawa <48723305+nockawa@users.noreply.github.com>"

# Map "Loïc Baumann" variations to "nockawa"
nockawa <48723305+nockawa@users.noreply.github.com> Loïc Baumann <loic.baumann@outlook.com>
nockawa <48723305+nockawa@users.noreply.github.com> Loic Baumann <loic.baumann@outlook.com>

# Map the unity3d.com email to the canonical noreply email
nockawa <48723305+nockawa@users.noreply.github.com> Loïc Baumann <loic.baumann@unity3d.com>

# Map the legacy GitHub noreply email (no numeric id) to the canonical one
nockawa <48723305+nockawa@users.noreply.github.com> nockawa <nockawa@users.noreply.github.com>

# Map commits authored as "nockawa" with the outlook.com email
nockawa <48723305+nockawa@users.noreply.github.com> nockawa <loic.baumann@outlook.com>

# Canonical identity (this line ensures "nockawa" commits stay as-is)
nockawa <48723305+nockawa@users.noreply.github.com>
